# Per-machine site → directory map for site-tmux.
# One `site=dir` per line. '~' expands to $HOME. Lines starting with '#' are ignored.
# This file is NOT committed — copy it to your config dir and edit per machine:
#   ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/site-tmux/sites.conf
#
# Any site not listed here (or running `site-tmux` with no argument) falls back to $HOME.
#
# Example (uncomment / adapt to the machine):
# obsidian-vault-api=/root/obsidian-vault-api
# vaults=/root/vaults
# myproject=~/code/myproject
#
# Optional: friendly label for this machine in claude.ai/code. Remote Control shows each
# device as <hostname>:<site>:<hash>; @prefix overrides the <hostname> segment for Claude
# only (remote-control runs in its own UTS namespace), leaving the real system hostname
# untouched. Reserved key — not a site. Needs root + `unshare`; otherwise it's ignored.
# @prefix=mybox
